- `c_i = (k + ord(p_i)) * G`
- `c_{i+12} = (k + ord(p_{i+12})) * G`

So `c_i - c_{i+12} = (ord(p_i) - ord(p_{i+12})) * G`. Since ord values are in 0-255, the difference is in -255..255. We can brute force this difference by checking which value gives a valid point.

